- op: discuss  # 5b05
  at: '2026-08-27T23:15:29Z'  # 5b05
  by: agent  # 5b05
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5b05
  clock: 3  # 5b05
  nonce: 5b05  # 5b05
  message: "GOVERNANCE APPROVAL REQUESTED. The fix touches .githooks/pre-push, which AGENTS.md lists as a governance path, so per the approval workflow no PR has been created. Requesting a ruling on two things: (1) exempt non-refs/heads pushes from the DCO block (two lines, same shape as the protected-branch check directly above it); (2) whether to push the 565 accumulated notes once the gate allows it -- that is additive and one-time, but it publishes commit bodies that have so far only ever existed locally. Found by reading the auto-pr log for PR #585 rather than by any failure: the run exited 0 and reported a clean merge."  # 5b05
- op: discuss  # 31b6
  at: '2026-08-30T02:37:20Z'  # 31b6
  by: agent  # 31b6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 31b6
  clock: 4  # 31b6
  nonce: 31b6  # 31b6
  message: "Recurred on PR #639 (2026-08-29). Same shape: the PR merged cleanly via rebase, then 'Attaching git note with original commit body' hit the pre-push DCO gate, which listed 43 'Notes added by git notes add' commits as missing a Signed-off-by. Two observations from this occurrence worth having on the item. (1) THE FAILURE IS SILENT AT THE EXIT CODE: auto-pr exited 0 despite the note push failing, so nothing surfaces unless you read the log -- and the log's tail shows the SUBSEQUENT git-pull collision, not this. (2) IT ONLY FIRES ON REBASE/SQUASH MERGES. Fast-forward merges preserve the body and skip the note step entirely, which is why this session's four earlier PRs did not hit it. Still needs_human_review: .githooks/pre-push is a governance file."  # 31b6
- op: discuss  # df9b
  at: '2026-09-12T19:31:28Z'  # df9b
  by: agent  # df9b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df9b
  clock: 5  # df9b
  nonce: df9b  # df9b
  message: "RE-ENCOUNTERED 2026-09-12 (PR #932 merge). Carrying forward what this occurrence adds; everything else here already said it, and this item remains the canonical row.\n\nUPDATED MEASUREMENT: 726 notes now (was 565 when this was filed 2026-08-27), depth 731, oldest still 2026-01-22, newest 2026-09-12. `git ls-remote origin | grep -c notes` -> 0. Unchanged conclusion, larger number.\n\nNEW, AND IT NAMES A SECOND FIX. This item says \"nothing downstream of the note-attach step checks whether the push landed\". The precise reason is scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh:2116-2117:\n\n    git push origin refs/notes/commits --quiet 2>/dev/null || \\\n    git push origin refs/notes/* --quiet 2>/dev/null || true\n\nstderr is discarded AND the failure is swallowed by `|| true`. So the invisibility is not an oversight downstream -- it is designed in at the push itself. The red BLOCKED banner is only ever visible because the hook writes to stdout, which `2>/dev/null` does not catch. That means even after the pre-push exemption lands, the NEXT breakage of this push would be equally silent. The fix has two limbs, not one:\n  (a) exempt refs/notes/ from the DCO block in .githooks/pre-push (this item already proposes it);\n  (b) keep the push non-fatal but report it on stderr instead of `2>/dev/null || true`, so a failure is visible on the first occurrence rather than the 726th.\n\nCONFIRMS the 2026-08-30 entry: it fires on the rebase/squash path. This occurrence was `merge-pr 932` doing a rebase merge.\n\nPROCESS NOTE, worth more than the defect. This has now been filed THREE times by three separate encounters, none of which found the prior: INV-nihaz (2026-08-27, 565 notes), WI-sahih (2026-09-02, \"NOT SIZED ... probably well behind\" -- which this item had already sized five days earlier), and INV-fapub (2026-09-12, mine). I filed mine without grepping the tracker, which is the project rule-1 failure exactly; the human asking \"is there any other open related tracker item?\" is what surfaced it. Three independent filings in sixteen days is a signal about discoverability, not about diligence: the three titles share almost no vocabulary (\"git-note body preservation\" / \"git-notes body preservation is unsatisfiable\" / \"git notes have NEVER been pushed\"), so a title search finds none of the others. `tracker clusters` would have.\n\nI am folding my own INV-fapub into this item. WI-sahih is a pre-existing item and its fold is the humans call, not mine -- proposed, not done."  # df9b
