- op: discuss  # dce2
  at: '2026-09-12T19:42:21Z'  # dce2
  by: agent  # dce2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dce2
  clock: 7  # dce2
  nonce: dce2  # dce2
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-09-12, PR #935, on behavioural evidence rather than proxy.\n\nHuman approved both halves of this items open question before anything was changed: (1) exempt refs/notes/ from the DCO gate, (2) push the accumulated backlog.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED, matching the two-line fix this item proposed plus the second limb found on the 2026-09-12 recurrence:\n  (a) .githooks/pre-push now skips the whole loop body for refs/notes/*. Safe because nothing in it applied: the protected-branch check strips refs/heads/ and was already inert on a notes ref, and the upstream workspace-file warning diffs paths a notes ref cannot contain.\n  (b) scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh no longer pushes with 2>/dev/null || true. That construct discarded the error text AND the exit status, which is the reason 726 consecutive failures produced no signal -- this item noted \"nothing downstream checks\", and the swallow was the mechanism. The push stays non-fatal (it must not fail a merge that already landed) but now reports on stderr, so the next breakage surfaces on the first occurrence rather than the 726th.\n\nEVIDENCE, each re-run of this items own filed repro:\n  1. BEFORE: git ls-remote origin refs/notes/* -> EMPTY (the measurement this item was filed on).\n     AFTER : 29d16785feff78d41a4a3214aacf1aff3e4153de  refs/notes/commits\n  2. git push origin refs/notes/commits -> \"* [new reference]  refs/notes/commits -> refs/notes/commits\", exit 0. The push this item called unsatisfiable by construction now succeeds.\n  3. THE DOCUMENTED RECOVERY PATH, which is what this item said was broken: a fresh git clone of the repo followed by the exact AGENTS.md command\n        git fetch origin refs/notes/*:refs/notes/*\n     yields \"notes in fresh clone: 727\". It fetched nothing before.\n  4. REGRESSION GUARD in .githooks/test_hooks.sh: the SAME unsigned commit that is blocked on refs/heads/t is asserted ALLOWED on refs/notes/commits, so the exemption cannot be silently reverted. 43 passed, 0 failed. CI runs this file.\n\nON THE BACKLOG PUBLICATION CONCERN this item raised (\"it publishes commit bodies that have so far only ever been local\"): checked before pushing rather than waved through. The repo is PUBLIC, so publish means publish. A 20-note sample showed the original commits are NOT ancestors of origin/dev (rebase/squash rewrote them), so the concern was real rather than imaginary. A secret-shaped scan over all 727 notes -- 26,926 lines, 1.5 MB -- for GitHub tokens, AWS keys, private-key headers, api_key/password assignments and the two project token names returned ZERO; the single password-pattern hit is a quoted git error string (\"Password authentication is not...\"). STATED LIMIT: that is a pattern scan, not a read of 26,926 lines, so it proves no secret-SHAPED content, not that nothing sensitive exists.\n\nNOT INVESTIGATED, carried forward from this item unchanged: whether the Woodpecker per-PR DCO gate would also reject a notes-ref push server-side. The hook never let a push reach the server before; now that it does, the push succeeded, so the server does not reject it. That open question is answered by (2) above.\n\nDUPLICATES: WI-sahih (2026-09-02) and INV-fapub (2026-09-12) are the same defect re-filed. INV-fapub is already folded here via duplicate_of. WI-sahih is a pre-existing work item and its fold remains the humans call."  # dce2
